Until 23 May, up-and-coming Düsseldorf Baskets can still submit documents to the arbitrating tribunal and prove its economic Bundesliga suitability.
So far, however, the Rhinelands have been denied the license twice.
Arbitration tribunal is the last instance.
Haigerloch: Lord's Supper church comes into focus
As a contribution of the city to the 150-year anniversary of the Evangelical Church in Haigerloch, the cultural and tourism office of the city dedicates the last of this year's public themed tours on Sunday, October 27, to the Lord's Supper Church.
After the visit to the Atorkeller-Museum, Haigerloch's period after 1850 is to be considered when Haigerloch came under Prussian rule.
Crowning conclusion is a visit to the Lord’s Supper Church.
There, the leaders are told the story of the construction of the church and gain insights into the development of the evangelical community in a thoroughly Catholic area.
Last but not least, in the church, there is also a view of the Lord’s Supper painting created by Friedrich Schüz with the support of Walter Kröll and Georg Halbritter.
It is an orginal reproduction of the famous Milanese model of Leonardo da Vinci.
Meeting point for the one-and-a-half-hour guided tour is at 3 p.m
Maps are available at the ticket office of the Atorkellermuseum.
For questions and information, please contact the Haigerloch tourist office.
