Nearly 100 African immigrants who wanted to enter Algeria die of thirst after two trucks remain in the middle of the Sahara.
Experts say that the violent crime, in which 14 adults and seven children died, is nothing but pure coincidence and not a sign of growing violence in America.
Instead of being unsettled by the U.S. government’s insolvency, investors focused on what presumably matters more: the Federal Reserve.
